IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-part9-duties`

-- Traces of the regulative rules of ccc12-part9-duties.l4. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT on the stable binary, so these are #TRACEs: no assertion
-- is counted here (0 written, 0 satisfied), and the outcome expected from the text is written beside each trace; the same duties are asserted through the decision functions in ccc12-tests-*.l4.
-- Expected, from the text: a MUST that the party performs is FULFILLED; a MUST that nothing has yet discharged stays outstanding (the text states no time limit, so there is no breach
-- to reach); where the gate is not JUST TRUE the rule states no duty and is FULFILLED outright; a MAY that is used is FULFILLED.

§ `Consecutive sentences, aggravating circumstances`
-- s 333.11(1): the court orders consecutive terms: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 333.11(1) the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 333.11 order that the sentence be served consecutively to the other sentence` AT 1
-- nothing done yet: the obligation stays outstanding
#TRACE `s 333.11(1) the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a witness` DOES `s 333.11 order that the sentence be served consecutively to the other sentence` AT 1
-- the duty does not arise: FULFILLED
#EVAL `s 333.11(1) the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST FALSE)
#TRACE `s 333.11(2) the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 333.11 order that the sentence be served consecutively to the other sentence` AT 1
#TRACE `s 346.1 the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 346.1 order that the sentence be served consecutively to the other sentence` AT 1
#EVAL `s 346.1 the court must order that the sentence be served consecutively` (JUST FALSE)
#TRACE `s 334.1(1) the court must consider the intent to sell or barter as an aggravating circumstance` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 334.1(1) consider as an aggravating circumstance the intent to sell or barter the stolen property or to fraudulently return it to a retail merchant` AT 1
#TRACE `s 334.1(2) the court must consider the interference with an essential infrastructure as an aggravating circumstance` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 334.1(2) consider as an aggravating circumstance the interference with an essential infrastructure` AT 1
#TRACE `s 346(1.4) the court must consider the sexual nature of the offence as an aggravating factor` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 346(1.4) consider as an aggravating factor that the offence was of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` AT 1
#TRACE `s 348.1 the court must consider the occupation of the dwelling-house as an aggravating circumstance` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 348.1 consider as an aggravating circumstance that the dwelling-house was occupied` AT 1
#EVAL `s 348.1 the court must consider the occupation of the dwelling-house as an aggravating circumstance` NOTHING

§ `The record of a sale of an automobile master key`
-- (a): the seller keeps the record: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 353(3)(a) the seller must keep a record of the transaction` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 353(3)(a) keep a record of the transaction showing the name and address of the purchaser and particulars of the licence issued to the purchaser` AT 1
-- (b): a peace officer asks and the seller produces the record: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 353(3)(b) the seller must produce the record for inspection at the request of a peace officer` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 353(3)(b) request the record for inspection` AT 1
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 353(3)(b) produce the record for inspection` AT 2
-- a peace officer asks and the seller has not yet produced it: the duty to produce is outstanding
#TRACE `s 353(3)(b) the seller must produce the record for inspection at the request of a peace officer` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 353(3)(b) request the record for inspection` AT 1

§ `Designation of a province for payday loans`
#TRACE `s 347.1(3) the Governor in Council must designate the province` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Governor in Council` DOES `s 347.1(3) designate the province by order` AT 1
#TRACE `s 347.1(4) the Governor in Council must revoke the designation` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Governor in Council` DOES `s 347.1(4) revoke the designation by order` AT 1
#EVAL `s 347.1(4) the Governor in Council must revoke the designation` (JUST FALSE)

§ `Powers`
#TRACE `s 327(2) the court may order the device forfeited to Her Majesty` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 327(2) order the device forfeited to Her Majesty` AT 1
#TRACE `s 339(3) the peace officer may enter the place` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `s 339(3) enter into or on the place to ascertain whether the lumber is detained there` AT 1
#TRACE `s 347(6) the accused may require the attendance of the actuary` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 347(6) require the attendance of the actuary for the purposes of cross-examination` AT 1
